  "id": "clearance",
  "term": "clearance",
  "definition": "In this context, clearance means the removal or handling of harmful material, such as protein aggregates, by cells in the brain. The article describes it as a function supported by microglial nanotubes, which can help cells dispose of or manage damaging substances.",
